The fonts are the latin and latin-ext subsets as served by Google Fonts, unchanged.

The body surface area formula is Mosteller's: R. D. Mosteller, "Simplified calculation of
body-surface area", New England Journal of Medicine 317 (1987), p. 1098.

Drug names are generic names used for realism. All doses, strengths and safe ranges in the
problems are practice numbers, not dosing information.

The blood gas rules, ranges and patient-communication guidance and their sources are listed in
docs/blood-gases.md (Sources) and REVIEW.md.
